<h1><span lang="EN-US">From 3 Entities</span></h1>
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-US">This command is accessible from</span> <b><i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Transformations &gt; From 3 Entities</b></span></i></b><span lang="EN-US">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">The command</span> <b><i style="font-weight:normal; font-style:normal;"><span class="Command">From 3 Entities</span></i></b> <span lang="EN-US">allows the user to create interactively transformation matrices using different definition methods. The</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Transformation</u></span> <span lang="EN-US">mode is displayed in a separated tab and the user can switch between all tabs, can make some changes or create new entities meanwhile. Each transformation matrix can be lately changed, applied to selection or activated for scanning.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">The Transformation tab contains 3 main sections:</span></p>
<table class="NormalTable" style="border-spacing:0px;" cellspacing="0">
<col class="whs4">
<col class="whs5">
<tr valign="middle" class="whs6">
<td rowspan="3" valign="top" width="236px" class="whs7">
<p class="whs8"><span lang="EN-US"><img src="../images/Create_transf.gif" width="227px" height="600px" border="0" class="img_whs9" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td valign="top" width="354px" class="whs10">
<p class="whs8"><span lang="EN-US">1. <a href="#Template_Section">Template section</a>  allows to save, modify and delete transformation templates</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="middle" class="whs6">
<td valign="top" width="354px" class="whs11">
<p class="whs8"><span lang="EN-US">2. <a href="#Setup_Transformation_Section">Setup Transformation section</a>  used to define transformation name and set entity correspondences.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="middle" class="whs6">
<td valign="top" width="354px" class="whs11">
<p class="whs8"><span lang="EN-US">3. <a href="#Define_Entity_Subsection">Define Entity sub-section</a>  used to set values for the chosen entity by different methods.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="Use"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>See also</b></span><span lang="EN-US">: Tutorials for creating transformations from 3 entities.</span></p>
<h2><span lang="EN-US"><a name="Template_Section"></a>Template section</span></h2>
<p><span lang="EN-US">In the KUBE software the transformations can be easily created and modified using templates. Currently there are 3 predefined transformation templates: 3-2-1, 3x3 points and 3x3 planes. If the user needs to create custom templates it is necessary to setup a transformation and then to save it with a new name.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">Each template can be loaded from the list in later sessions of KUBE.</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>:</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">In a template are saved both the correspondences and their values. Modifications in each existing template can be updated by using the button</span> <span class="Button">Save</span><span lang="EN-US">.</span></p>
<h2><span lang="EN-US"><a name="Setup_Transformation_Section"></a>Setup Transformation section</span></h2>
<p><span lang="EN-US">In this section all entity correspondences should be set. Description:</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Source Entities</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Movable datums (if the transformation is applied on these datums, their positions should be identical with the correspondent target entities). Generally the source entities belong to the movable entity or can be captured for future scanning.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Target Entities</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Fixed datums. Usually, the target entities are extracted from a CAD model or a reference mesh.</span></p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a7" style="text-decoration:underline;">Schematic</a>:</span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP290485387" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><span lang="EN-US"><img src="../images/image018.gif" width="497px" height="171px" border="0" class="img_whs12" alt=""></span></p>
</div>
<p><span lang="EN-US">For each correspondence should be chosen one pair of primitives. Click on the arrow button next to the datum button to select the appropriate primitive from the list:</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US"><img src="../images/Choose_datum.gif" width="139px" height="177px" border="0" class="img_whs13" alt=""></span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">The last option "Pick from screen" in this list allows the user to pick an entity from the viewport. If this option is enabled, then the user can simultaneously select entity type and define its values. It is used for quick source or target entity definition by picking predefined datums from the viewport. By default this option is disabled and each primitive must be defined by any of the available methods. Detailed description of the process follows in the <i>Define Entity sub-section.</i></span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">Both source and target entities should have datums of similar type.</span></p>
<p class="ExampleCode"><span lang="EN-US">For example:</span></p>
<p class="ExampleCode"><span lang="EN-US">Point to point or point to circle is a valid correspondence. It will be marked by <img src="../images/image020.gif" width="17px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs14" alt=""></span></p>
<p class="ExampleCode"><span lang="EN-US">Point to line or line to plane is not a valid correspondence and it will be marked by <img src="../images/image021.gif" width="17px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs14" alt="">. If one or more invalid correspondences are present, transformation can not be created.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">On the left of each datum button there is a small icon showing the definition method used to set values for this datum. The meaning of each icon is explained in the table below:</span></p>
<table cellspacing="0" width="75%" class="whs15">
<col class="whs16">
<col class="whs17">
<tr valign="top" class="whs18">
<td width="8.477%" class="whs19">
<p class="whs8"><span lang="EN-US"><img src="../images/sel2.gif" width="23px" height="19px" border="0" class="img_whs20" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td width="91.523%" class="whs21">
<p class="whs8"><span lang="EN-US">The values for this datum are manually input or picked as points directly from the viewport.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs18">
<td width="8.477%" class="whs22">
<p class="whs8"><span lang="EN-US"><img src="../images/sel2_red.gif" width="23px" height="20px" border="0" class="img_whs23" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td width="91.523%" class="whs24">
<p class="whs8"><span lang="EN-US">The values for this datum are not yet defined.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs18">
<td width="8.477%" class="whs22">
<p class="whs8"><span lang="EN-US"><img src="../images/sel1.gif" width="23px" height="22px" border="0" class="img_whs25" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td width="91.523%" class="whs24">
<p class="whs8"><span lang="EN-US">The datum is chosen from a list or picked as primitive from the viewport</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs18">
<td width="8.477%" class="whs22">
<p class="whs8"><span lang="EN-US"><img src="../images/sel3.gif" width="21px" height="20px" border="0" class="img_whs26" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td width="91.523%" class="whs24">
<p class="whs8"><span lang="EN-US">The values are set by fitting datum to a custom selection</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs18">
<td width="8.477%" class="whs27">
<p class="whs8"><span lang="EN-US"><img src="../images/sel4.gif" width="20px" height="20px" border="0" class="img_whs28" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td width="91.523%" class="whs24">
<p class="whs8"><span lang="EN-US">The values will be defined lately during capture procedure.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p id="P2">&#160;</p>
<p class="Note" id="P2"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note:</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">If there are not defined values, the correspondence can not be created.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">When all the three correspondences are set and their primitives defined, it remains only to choose a name for this transformation.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Name</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">You have 3 choices for setting the transformation name: leave the default one, type a new name or choose an existing one from the list. <i style="font-style:normal;">The default name is Transformation N, where N is the number of the subsequent newly created transformation. When a transformation</i></span> <span lang="EN-US"><i style="font-style:normal;">is created the number N in the name will automatically increase.</i></span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">When ready press the Create button. If the transformation is successfully created a message will appear asking you whether to activate the transformation for scanning or not. In case of answering Yes, have in mind that all further scanning will pass through the transformation matrix and the co-ordinates of the captured points will not be in global space.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">If you want to exit the transformation mode, then press the</span> <span class="Button">Close</span> <span lang="EN-US">button.</span></p>
<h2><span lang="EN-US"><a name="Define_Entity_Subsection"></a>Define Entity sub-section</span></h2>
<p><span lang="EN-US">The definition dialog shown in this sub-section depends on the chosen target or source entity. Each datum definition can be set by 4 main methods:</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Capture</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Delayed operation. It will start when all correspondences are set and Create transformation is initiated. The datums will be captured by order of their correspondences. The capturing functionality is the same as in the arm menu.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Fit to selection</span></b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Interactive method for setting values. The user makes a selection, press the button Fit selection and the datum parameters will be instantly filled in the edit boxes. If necessary these values can be manually changed.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Choose from list or pick entity</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Both options refer to the same functionality  selection of an existing primitive, co-ordinate axis or plane. The user can either choose a datum from the list or directly pick it on the viewport. The datum parameters will be instantly filled in the edit boxes. If necessary these values can be manually changed.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Manual co-ordinates input or pick points</span></b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Both options refer to the same functionality  simple co-ordinate input. The user can either type manually the datum parameters in the edit boxes or pick a minimal number of points on the viewport to define the datum. The minimal number of picked points depends on the entity type.</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="P3"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note:</b></span> If you want to use <span class="Command">Pick points</span> method for datum definition and at the same time you have an active selection mode, you should first exit the selection mode by using the key <span class="Button">Esc</span> and KUBE will pass automatically to the <span class="Mode">Pick points</span> mode</p>
<p><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Particularities</b></span>: For each entity definition a method is automatically selected using the following rule:</p>
<ul type="circle" class="whs29">
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p">
<p class="whs30">Pick from viewport method is enabled by default only the first time you open the transformation mode.</p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p">
<p class="whs30">If the user changes the definition method for an entity, his last choice will be set as active by default when switching to another entity definition (no matter source or target).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-US">When an entity is defined it appears in the viewport as temporary datum. Dialog description for each entity type:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US"><a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_point.htm" id="a1">Point</a></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US"><a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_line.htm" id="a2">Line</a></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US"><a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_plane.htm" id="a3">Plane</a></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US"><a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_cylinder.htm" id="a4">Cylinder</a></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US"><a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_sphere.htm" id="a5">Sphere</a></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US"><a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_circle.htm" id="a6">Circle</a></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="P4"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Notes</b></span><span lang="EN-US">: The algorithm for transformation creation tries to find exact correspondence between the given entities. That is why there are certain restrictions for the direction, in which the source or target entities can be moved towards the other source or target entities respectively, in the scene. Here follow the list of all entities and their possible movements:<br>
*</span> <b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">Point &#160;- the correspondence between source and target points should be exact or very close.<br>
*</span></b> <b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">Line - the target or source line can be moved along its tangent only. It should not be offset.<br>
*</span></b> <b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">Circle -</span></b> <b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">the correspondence between source and target circles should be exact or very close. The radius can vary.<br>
*</span></b> <b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">Plane -</span></b> <b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">the target or source plane can be moved along its surface only. It should not be offset along its normal.<br>
*</span></b> <b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">Sphere</span></b><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">- the correspondence between source and target spheres should be exact or very close. The radius can vary.<br>
*</span></b> <b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">Cylinder</span></b><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">- the target or source cylinder can be moved along its tangent only. It should not be offset.</span></b></p>
<p id="P10" class="whs31"><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;"><a href="javascript:void(0);" onclick="var e; if (parseInt(navigator.appVersion)&gt;=4){e=event;} if (parseInt(navigator.appVersion) &gt;=2 &amp;&amp; typeof(PopupMenu_Invoke) == 'function') PopupMenu_Invoke(e,'','3-2-1 Transformation','create_3-2-1_transformation.htm','From N Constrained Points','from_n_constrained_points.htm','From N Points','from_n_points.htm','From Single Plane','create_from_single_plane.htm','From Viewport','create_from_viewport.htm','Interactive Transformation','Interactive_Transformation.htm','Type In Transformation','Type_In_Transformation.htm');return false;" title=""><img src="../images/ss_btn_see_also.gif" border="0" height="17" width="60" alt=""></a></span></b></p>

